    "text": "We had some high school interns that were top of the class and they couldn't figure out how to do the handwritten time sheets properly. Finally, I pulled the analog clock off the wall, put it on a desk and pulled a bunch of quarters out of the petty cash along with a dollar bill. Asked them how many quarters in a dollar. We all agreed it was four. Put a quarter on the 12, 3, 6 and 9. Told them Bill came in at 10:15 and left at 12:30. How many quarters was that? Once they figured that out, I had the convert it into dollars. Once they got it, they understood. No more calls from Payroll. Yeah.",
